cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "QACD: Question-Conditioned Atomic Claim Decomposition for LVLM answer-error risk scoring"
abstract: >-
  QACD is a post-hoc answer-error risk scorer for frozen vision-language models on
  visual question answering. It decomposes an answer into question-conditioned
  atomic claims, collects belief-consistency, direct-verification, alignment and
  mechanical-OCR evidence, calibrates a regularised logistic risk map, and
  aggregates claim risks into an answer-level score with a maximum operator.
  The pipeline is evaluated on a frozen TextVQA test split of 1,999 responses
  over 1,278 unseen images. Numerical results are a project deliverable and are
  not published in this repository.
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-24"
license: LicenseRef-Proprietary
